### Phase 4 — auth smoke tests
# Get a token from the browser console on the running client while signed in:
#   await window.Clerk.session.getToken()
# Then paste it below. Tokens are short-lived (~60s), so refresh when you get 401.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@citizenToken = paste_citizen_token_here
@adminToken = paste_admin_token_here

### 1. No token → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me

### 2. Citizen token → 200 { data: { id, role: "citizen" } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}

### 3. Admin token → 200 { data: { id, role: "admin" } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4. Admin route with a citizen token → 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}

### 5. Admin route with an admin token → 200 { data: { ok: true } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6. Garbage token → 401 UNAUTHORIZED (not 500)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token
